WEBVTT

00:01.927 --> 00:03.751
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:06.264 --> 00:08.297
- Damn it!
- You all right, brother?

00:08.391 --> 00:10.341
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:10.435 --> 00:12.802
- I'm training.
- You're training for what?

00:12.896 --> 00:15.138
For a race around the world.

00:17.567 --> 00:19.684
- Jack.
- I'm Desmond.

00:20.862 --> 00:23.021
See you in another life, yeah?

00:41.591 --> 00:44.917
Type in exactly what I tell you,
understand? Nothing else.

00:45.011 --> 00:48.629
4... 8...

00:50.100 --> 00:52.008
15...

00:52.102 --> 00:53.176
16...

00:54.980 --> 00:56.387
23...

00:57.857 --> 00:59.234
42.

00:59.317 --> 01:00.808
Now press "Execute."

01:00.902 --> 01:03.572
- What's gonna happen?
- Just push it!

01:04.030 --> 01:06.105
Kate! Locke!

01:06.658 --> 01:08.941
Who the hell is that?

01:10.829 --> 01:12.737
Move and I kill him.

01:30.307 --> 01:33.143
- Michael! Sawyer!
- Jin!

01:37.689 --> 01:40.598
Others! Others! Others!

01:41.443 --> 01:42.715
- What?
- Others.

02:34.996 --> 02:37.071
Where's my boy?

02:37.874 --> 02:39.991
Where's my boy?

02:40.335 --> 02:41.743
Hey!

02:41.836 --> 02:45.371
Hey, what did you do with my boy?
You hear me?

02:45.465 --> 02:47.008
Come back here!

02:49.803 --> 02:52.503
Do you want him to die? Put it down.

02:58.687 --> 03:02.472
Is this what you were talking about,
Locke? Is this your destiny?

03:05.860 --> 03:08.102
"All roads lead here".

03:10.365 --> 03:12.648
My mother stole again from me this week.

03:12.909 --> 03:16.402
I don't even keep money in my purse
anymore, I've been hiding it.

03:16.871 --> 03:19.280
But when she wants a drink...

03:20.166 --> 03:22.075
She stole 30 dollars.

03:22.919 --> 03:26.037
I know it may not seem like
a lot of money to some of you,

03:26.131 --> 03:29.457
but it's a lot to me.
And I want it back.

03:32.596 --> 03:34.921
Something you want to say?

03:36.516 --> 03:40.051
John, you've been coming here
for a month now...

03:40.145 --> 03:43.596
I just don't think 30 dollars
is worth getting angry about.

03:43.690 --> 03:45.515
Francine feels 30 dollars...

03:45.609 --> 03:48.226
Francine feels a little too much,
if you ask me.

03:48.320 --> 03:50.395
You all do.

03:51.072 --> 03:54.649
I mean, seriously...
"So-and-so never called me back."

03:54.743 --> 03:58.736
"My mother stole 30 dollars."
I never even knew who my parents were.

03:59.831 --> 04:03.157
Couple years ago,
my birth mother found me.

04:03.251 --> 04:05.410
And...

04:05.503 --> 04:07.578
she told me...

04:09.633 --> 04:11.708
I was special.

04:13.970 --> 04:18.965
And through her I met my real father.
Great news, right?

04:19.601 --> 04:23.469
Well, he pretended to love me,
just long enough to steal my kidney,

04:23.563 --> 04:25.555
because he had to have a transplant.

04:25.649 --> 04:29.183
And then he dropped me back
in the world like a piece of trash,

04:29.277 --> 04:32.030
just like he did
on the day that I was born.

04:33.907 --> 04:37.817
You want your damn 30 dollars back?
I want my kidney back!

04:48.546 --> 04:50.955
Probably a good idea.

04:52.092 --> 04:55.418
You know if you get kidney cancer,
you've only got one.

04:56.388 --> 04:58.463
That's funny.

05:00.517 --> 05:02.633
I'm sorry if I ruined your meeting.

05:02.727 --> 05:06.721
Oh, hell. You just said everything
I've always wanted to say in there.

05:06.815 --> 05:10.860
Most of the time, I want to stand up
and scream "Get over it, freaks!"

05:10.944 --> 05:14.228
- Well, why don't you?
- Ah, I have to keep a cork in.

05:14.322 --> 05:17.690
Once I get all hot and bothered,
there's no stopping me.

05:20.579 --> 05:23.446
Guess you won't be coming back
next week, huh?

05:23.540 --> 05:25.615
No, not likely.

05:25.709 --> 05:28.545
That's too bad. I like bald guys.

05:29.671 --> 05:32.080
- I'm not bald.
- I can wait.

05:36.636 --> 05:39.306
I'm Helen, by the way.

05:40.890 --> 05:43.174
Hi, Helen. I'm John.

05:45.604 --> 05:47.178
Where's Kate?

05:47.272 --> 05:50.056
Lower your gun
or I'll blow his damned head off.

05:50.150 --> 05:52.308
Where's Kate?

06:42.077 --> 06:44.569
- Put it down.
- I'm not putting down anything!

06:44.663 --> 06:46.696
Jack, calm down. It's OK.

06:54.256 --> 06:55.663
- Do not move!
- Don't...

06:55.757 --> 06:57.300
- What?
- He's unarmed...

06:57.384 --> 06:59.625
He just had a gun pointed at your head!

07:03.390 --> 07:05.465
What did you do?

07:06.977 --> 07:09.260
What did you do?

07:13.191 --> 07:15.266
We're all gonna die.

07:19.906 --> 07:21.981
We're all gonna die.

07:42.512 --> 07:45.348
- I have to fix it.
- What the hell's he talking about?

07:45.432 --> 07:48.268
Listen! If you do not let me up,
we are going to die.

07:48.351 --> 07:52.178
- Stop moving, or, I swear to God...
- Look at the wall! You see that?

07:52.981 --> 07:55.223
That's a timer and it's counting down.

07:57.152 --> 07:59.852
I've got to enter the code,
got to push the button.

07:59.946 --> 08:01.729
- Or what?
- Jack, let him up.

08:01.823 --> 08:04.315
Don't tell me what to do. Or what?

08:04.993 --> 08:07.402
What's going to happen?

08:08.538 --> 08:10.697
Do I know you?

08:17.505 --> 08:19.163
You got him?

08:28.433 --> 08:30.133
Bastard!

08:34.022 --> 08:36.347
- What?
- Nothing, Jack.

08:52.332 --> 08:53.792
Hey.

08:54.709 --> 08:56.868
What are you doing?

09:00.173 --> 09:02.457
- Where are you going?
- Nowhere. I...

09:04.636 --> 09:09.130
I... just have trouble
sleeping in a strange bed.

09:12.018 --> 09:15.960
It has nothing to do with you, Helen.
I promise. I really like you.

09:19.567 --> 09:21.851
I'm sorry, I'll call you later.

09:45.302 --> 09:46.876
Morning.

09:48.179 --> 09:49.504
Morning.

09:50.640 --> 09:53.966
John, I know you like to drive
through my neighbourhood.

09:54.060 --> 09:59.055
And I know that every now and then,
you like to park outside my house.

10:01.067 --> 10:04.977
Now, I thought it might all stop when
I moved, but here you are.

10:07.240 --> 10:10.233
Now, I'll admit,
at first I thought it was funny.

10:12.037 --> 10:14.362
Now it's just annoying.

10:14.456 --> 10:17.407
So how about you tell me
what the hell it is you want.

10:22.172 --> 10:25.748
- Why?
- Excuse me?

10:28.511 --> 10:30.055
Why?

10:38.396 --> 10:40.471
There is no "why".

10:41.816 --> 10:45.018
You think you're the first person
that ever got conned?

10:45.111 --> 10:47.979
You needed a father figure
and I needed a kidney.

10:48.073 --> 10:51.065
And that's what happened.

10:51.159 --> 10:53.234
Get over it.

10:55.455 --> 10:57.989
And, John, don't come back.

11:00.585 --> 11:02.910
You're not wanted.

11:26.361 --> 11:28.519
I don't think you need that, Kate.

11:32.867 --> 11:35.568
Whatever you're looking for,
maybe I can help.

11:35.662 --> 11:37.779
Can you fix a computer?

11:38.331 --> 11:41.324
- Then you can't help me.
- Sayid can fix a computer.

11:42.502 --> 11:46.788
- Get him. Go and get Sayid.
- Can you get back up that rope?

11:46.881 --> 11:49.165
There's got to be a front door here.

11:49.259 --> 11:53.169
Down the corridor to the left.
Be persistent, the wheel sticks.

11:55.223 --> 11:56.683
Got ya!

12:12.407 --> 12:16.317
- Now, tell me what's going on.
- We don't have time...

12:16.411 --> 12:19.320
- We're taking a time-out.
- Please, just let me...

12:19.414 --> 12:21.906
You wanna get to work?
Tell me how you got here.

12:23.126 --> 12:26.536
It was three years ago.
I was on a solo race around the world,

12:26.630 --> 12:29.466
and my boat crashed into the reef
and Kelvin came.

12:29.549 --> 12:32.250
- Kelvin?
- He comes runnin' out the jungle,

12:32.344 --> 12:34.377
"Hurry! Hurry! Come with me!"

12:35.430 --> 12:37.338
He brings me down here.

12:37.974 --> 12:40.341
First thing he does,
cos it's beeping,

12:40.435 --> 12:43.271
he types in the code,
pushes the button and it stops.

12:46.566 --> 12:48.850
"What was all that about?" I say.

12:49.444 --> 12:51.978
"Just saving the world", he says.

12:54.366 --> 12:57.442
- "Saving the world?"
- His words, not mine.

13:00.622 --> 13:02.864
So I started pushing the button too.

13:03.792 --> 13:07.285
And we saved the world together
for a while, and that was lovely.

13:07.379 --> 13:10.663
Then Kelvin died.
And now here I am all alone.

13:15.262 --> 13:16.534
The end!

13:30.527 --> 13:33.061
Don't tell me you believe this.
This is crazy.

13:33.154 --> 13:35.907
You think that makes sense?
Pushing a button?

13:36.491 --> 13:40.568
- You're going to take his word for it?
- His word is all we have, Jack.

13:41.788 --> 13:44.947
You don't have to take my word for it.
Watch the film.

13:47.210 --> 13:50.078
- What?
- The bookcase. Top shelf.

13:50.338 --> 13:53.748
Behind <i>Turn of The Screw.</i>
Projector's in the pantry.

14:28.752 --> 14:30.410
Here...

14:33.214 --> 14:37.125
Dude, I gotta say, I didn't think
we were gonna get through the night.

14:38.219 --> 14:41.254
And I wasn't even here
for that baby-stealing part.

14:41.932 --> 14:44.090
I can assure you it was very exciting.

14:44.184 --> 14:46.749
Things are finally returning
to normalness.

14:46.853 --> 14:48.886
Sayid!

14:49.856 --> 14:51.055
Aw, crap.

14:52.734 --> 14:55.143
Sayid! We need your help.

15:03.119 --> 15:05.820
What do you know?
What'd they do to you?

15:05.914 --> 15:09.407
Who the hell are they?
Who the hell are they?

15:12.170 --> 15:13.953
Others!

15:15.715 --> 15:18.499
- Did you see Walt?
- The Others? How many?

15:19.970 --> 15:21.242
How many?

15:23.598 --> 15:26.758
- They had him blindfolded. Blindfolded.
- Yes!

15:26.851 --> 15:29.552
Could be a hundred of them out there!

15:33.400 --> 15:35.224
- Push me up.
- What?

15:35.318 --> 15:38.519
Push me up.
I wanna try and get us outta here.

15:40.699 --> 15:42.774
C'mon, help us out, Chewie.

15:59.050 --> 16:03.263
They got it weighted down with
something. It's tied off somewhere.

16:05.390 --> 16:07.215
Come on, lift me higher.

16:46.640 --> 16:48.715
It's a girl.

16:56.733 --> 17:00.601
Wanna tell me what was going on
down here before I showed up, John?

17:01.071 --> 17:05.690
Kate was tied up. Desmond had a gun on
me. I think you caught the gist of it.

17:08.411 --> 17:09.986
Desmond.

17:11.706 --> 17:13.948
He wanted to know a lot about us.

17:14.042 --> 17:16.367
How we got here. If we were sick.

17:16.461 --> 17:19.996
- You didn't ask anything about him?
- He was the one with the gun.

17:20.090 --> 17:24.542
You seem calm for someone who believes
the world's going to end in 45 minutes.

17:24.636 --> 17:26.544
He'll fix it.

17:28.348 --> 17:32.967
You understand that what he's saying,
it's insane. It's impossible.

17:33.061 --> 17:35.011
Why is it insane?

17:36.189 --> 17:39.349
The last time I saw the computer
that would save the world,

17:39.442 --> 17:40.850
it didn't look like that.

17:40.944 --> 17:44.437
Is the reason you're so upset
because he said he recognised you?

17:52.539 --> 17:55.156
Because that would be impossible.

18:20.025 --> 18:24.560
<i>Welcome. I'm Dr Marvin Candle</i>,
<i>and this is the orientation film</i>

18:24.654 --> 18:27.563
<i>for Station Three</i>
<i>of the Dharma Initiative.</i>

18:27.657 --> 18:31.025
<i>In a moment</i>, <i>you'll be given</i>
<i>a simple set of instructions</i>

18:31.119 --> 18:34.612
<i>for how you and your partner</i>
<i>will fulfil the responsibilities</i>

18:34.706 --> 18:38.241
<i>associated with this station.</i>
<i>But first</i>, <i>a little history.</i>

18:39.044 --> 18:42.412
<i>The Dharma Initiative</i>
<i>was created in 1970</i>

18:42.505 --> 18:45.665
<i>and is the brainchild</i>
<i>of Gerald and Karen DeGroot</i>,

18:45.759 --> 18:48.876
<i>two doctoral candidates</i>
<i>at the University of Michigan.</i>

18:48.970 --> 18:52.912
<i>Following in the footsteps</i>
<i>of visionaries such as BF Skinner...</i>

18:53.016 --> 18:56.801
<i>...imagined a large-scale</i>
<i>communal research compound</i>

18:56.895 --> 19:01.347
<i>where scientists and free-thinkers from</i>
<i>around the globe could pursue research</i>

19:01.483 --> 19:07.353
<i>in meteorology</i>, <i>psychology</i>,
<i>parapsychology</i>, <i>zoology</i>,

19:07.447 --> 19:10.857
<i>electromagnetism</i>,
<i>and utopian social...</i>

19:10.951 --> 19:15.278
<i>...reclusive Danish industrialist</i>
<i>and munitions magnate Alvar Hanso</i>,

19:15.455 --> 19:17.780
<i>whose financial backing made their dream</i>

19:17.874 --> 19:22.243
<i>of a multi-purpose social science</i>
<i>research facility a reality.</i>

19:23.255 --> 19:27.623
<i>You and your partner are currently</i>
<i>located in Station Three</i>, <i>or "The Swan"</i>,

19:27.717 --> 19:30.282
<i>and will be for the next 540 days.</i>

19:30.929 --> 19:34.213
<i>Station Three was originally constructed</i>
<i>as a laboratory</i>

19:34.307 --> 19:36.674
<i>where scientists</i>
<i>could work to understand</i>

19:36.768 --> 19:39.302
<i>the unique electromagnetic fluctuations</i>

19:39.396 --> 19:41.721
<i>emanating from this sector</i>
<i>of the island.</i>

19:42.774 --> 19:48.353
<i>Not long after the experiments began</i>,
<i>however</i>, <i>there was... an incident.</i>

19:49.656 --> 19:53.066
<i>Since that time</i>, <i>the following</i>
<i>protocol has been observed.</i>

19:53.910 --> 19:57.852
<i>Every 108 minutes</i>,
<i>the button must be pushed.</i>

19:58.623 --> 20:01.074
<i>From the moment the alarm sounds</i>,

20:01.167 --> 20:06.204
<i>you will have four minutes to enter the</i>
<i>code into the microcomputer processor...</i>

20:06.298 --> 20:08.414
<i>...induction into the programme.</i>

20:08.508 --> 20:13.544
<i>When the alarm sounds</i>, <i>either you</i>
<i>or your partner must input the code.</i>

20:14.347 --> 20:18.560
<i>It is highly recommended that you and</i>
<i>your partner take alternating shifts.</i>

20:18.685 --> 20:21.678
<i>In this manner</i>,
<i>you will both stay as fresh and alert...</i>

20:21.771 --> 20:24.555
<i>...utmost importance</i>
<i>that when the alarm sounds</i>,

20:24.649 --> 20:28.434
<i>the code be entered correctly</i>
<i>and in a timely fashion.</i>

20:28.528 --> 20:32.271
<i>Do not attempt to use</i>
<i>the computer for anything...</i>

20:32.908 --> 20:34.649
<i>Congratulations!</i>

20:34.743 --> 20:39.612
<i>Until your replacements arrive</i>, <i>the</i>
<i>future of the project is in your hands.</i>

20:39.706 --> 20:42.949
<i>On behalf of the DeGroots</i>, <i>Alvar Hanso</i>,

20:43.043 --> 20:45.410
<i>and all of us at the Dharma Initiative</i>,

20:45.503 --> 20:50.623
<i>thank you</i>, namaste,
<i>and good luck.</i>

21:03.772 --> 21:06.014
We're gonna need to watch that again.

21:10.987 --> 21:12.812
What's that?

21:12.906 --> 21:17.608
It's a present. It's been six months.
Sort of an anniversary, right?

21:21.164 --> 21:23.865
- I didn't get you anything.
- That's OK.

21:23.959 --> 21:26.242
Only cost me a buck.

21:35.595 --> 21:39.005
It's to my place.
Thought you might be tired of knocking.

21:43.353 --> 21:45.219
Well, Helen, I...

21:45.939 --> 21:47.263
I don't know what to say.

21:49.317 --> 21:52.435
There's just one condition though, John.

21:53.697 --> 21:57.148
When you stay over, you stay over.

21:58.159 --> 21:59.192
What do you mean?

22:00.870 --> 22:02.695
I followed you last night.

22:03.582 --> 22:06.115
To that house that you go to.

22:08.128 --> 22:10.078
Is it your father's house?

22:17.262 --> 22:20.296
Why would you follow me, Helen?
Why would you do that?

22:21.224 --> 22:23.466
You sneak off
in the middle of the night.

22:23.560 --> 22:25.927
I just needed to know
where you were going.

22:26.021 --> 22:27.397
I care about you, John...

22:27.480 --> 22:30.098
But what I do is my business.
It's personal.

22:30.191 --> 22:33.768
I wasted 20 years of my life
being angry.

22:34.946 --> 22:39.649
I told myself I would get over it,
but I... I couldn't do it alone.

22:41.870 --> 22:43.945
I needed to find help.

22:46.750 --> 22:48.825
You help me, John.

22:51.212 --> 22:53.663
And I can help you.

22:54.424 --> 22:58.553
You just have to promise me that you're
not gonna go to that place anymore.

23:03.224 --> 23:04.716
All right.

23:06.353 --> 23:08.136
All right?

23:32.587 --> 23:35.152
You're going to watch that again?

23:36.299 --> 23:40.241
- Aren't you?
- No, John. I'm not.

24:00.615 --> 24:02.075
OK, OK!

24:02.158 --> 24:04.275
You all right, sister?

24:06.705 --> 24:10.073
- Who are you?
- We crashed here.

24:10.166 --> 24:13.242
We were on a plane.
Sydney to Los Angeles...

24:14.796 --> 24:17.549
- What?
- 40 of us made it.

24:21.511 --> 24:23.753
Flight 815?

24:26.600 --> 24:28.675
You were on it, too?

24:29.853 --> 24:32.053
What? You were in the back?

24:34.983 --> 24:38.643
- It broke off mid-air, how did you...
- I don't know, I don't know.

24:38.737 --> 24:41.302
The plane came apart

24:41.406 --> 24:45.858
and somebody's fricking hardside came
out of the overhead and knocked me out.

24:45.952 --> 24:48.111
I woke up underwater and...

24:49.122 --> 24:52.156
made my way to the top. Swam to shore.

24:54.252 --> 24:57.870
You been out here by yourself
all this time?

24:58.965 --> 25:03.209
Trying to find food. Making my way,
hoping to find somebody...

25:04.596 --> 25:07.349
And then, yesterday, they found me.

25:07.432 --> 25:09.882
- Who are they?
- You tell me.

25:09.976 --> 25:14.387
Did you see a boy? Ten years old?
They took my son.

25:16.650 --> 25:19.142
No. I'm sorry.

25:20.987 --> 25:23.771
- I'm Ana Lucia.
- Sawyer.

25:24.866 --> 25:26.941
This is Mike.

25:27.702 --> 25:30.069
The quiet Korean guy's Jin.

25:31.248 --> 25:34.657
We're about to be the best thing
that ever happened to you.

25:34.751 --> 25:36.409
How's that?

25:36.503 --> 25:39.120
Next time Shaft opens the cage,

25:40.507 --> 25:43.624
he's gonna get a surprising little
"howdy-doody".

25:51.309 --> 25:53.926
Are you in contact with the people
who made it?

25:54.020 --> 25:56.721
The film?
Are you in contact with anyone?

25:57.524 --> 25:59.766
Do you think I'd be here if I was?

26:01.319 --> 26:05.146
How is it that you didn't know
about the crash? About us?

26:06.658 --> 26:10.276
I push this button every 108 minutes.

26:11.496 --> 26:13.821
I don't get out much.

26:14.708 --> 26:16.783
So these replacements...

26:17.669 --> 26:21.037
Kelvin died
waiting for his replacements.

26:22.924 --> 26:27.001
So you don't get out, you don't see
anyone, where's your food come from?

26:27.554 --> 26:30.838
- You really think this is happening?
- Why wouldn't it be?

26:32.809 --> 26:36.751
It says "Quarantine" on the inside
of the hatch to keep you down here,

26:36.855 --> 26:39.138
keep you scared. But you know what?

26:39.232 --> 26:42.517
We've been up there for over 40 days
and no one's gotten sick.

26:42.611 --> 26:45.280
You think this is the only part of it
that's true?

26:45.363 --> 26:49.232
Did you ever think they put you here
to push a button every 100 minutes

26:49.326 --> 26:52.360
just to see if you would?
That the computer, the button,

26:52.454 --> 26:55.071
it's just a mind game? An experiment?

26:57.000 --> 26:59.367
Every single day.

27:06.051 --> 27:08.751
And for all our sakes,
I hope it's not real.

27:11.890 --> 27:15.550
But the film says this is
an electromagnetic station.

27:15.644 --> 27:17.927
And I dunno about you, brother,

27:18.021 --> 27:22.265
but every time I walk past that concrete
wall out there, my fillings hurt.

27:26.571 --> 27:28.396
Right.

27:41.544 --> 27:43.786
Oh, no!

27:43.880 --> 27:45.621
What happened?

27:51.554 --> 27:53.755
It's over.

27:59.437 --> 28:01.554
What do you mean "It's over"?

28:14.953 --> 28:18.404
What are you doing? Are you leaving?

28:19.249 --> 28:21.532
Desmond. Wait.

28:24.296 --> 28:27.747
We can fix the computer.
Sayid is coming. He knows...

28:27.841 --> 28:29.957
Give him my best.

28:38.518 --> 28:41.511
Wait, wait! Where are you...
You can't leave!

28:43.440 --> 28:45.390
Where are you going?

28:45.483 --> 28:47.642
As far as I can run, brother.

28:55.201 --> 28:57.276
- What should we do?
- Nothing.

28:58.246 --> 29:00.863
We do nothing. It's not real.
None of it's real.

29:00.957 --> 29:03.574
No...
This isn't what was supposed to happen.

29:05.629 --> 29:07.704
What was supposed to happen?

29:07.797 --> 29:13.219
- Please! Don't leave me here.
- Goodbye, John. You're on your own.

29:13.303 --> 29:14.377
Jack.

29:44.542 --> 29:46.200
Damn it!

29:47.045 --> 29:50.121
Why is this happening like this?
What do you want?

29:53.218 --> 29:55.585
What am I supposed to do?

30:43.184 --> 30:44.842
Helen, what...

30:44.936 --> 30:48.012
Helen, what...
Hey, Helen, wait.

30:48.857 --> 30:51.099
Helen! Don't!

30:51.192 --> 30:52.850
Helen!

30:56.323 --> 30:57.939
Why are you doing this?

30:58.033 --> 31:01.567
He's not coming out of his house
because he doesn't care.

31:01.661 --> 31:05.029
I know why you're here,
why you keep coming here.

31:05.123 --> 31:10.576
You're scared. You're scared of moving
forward, with me, with us.

31:13.506 --> 31:15.498
You're gonna have to choose.

31:16.927 --> 31:18.918
Him or me.

31:21.640 --> 31:24.173
No, no. No, it's not that simple.

31:24.267 --> 31:25.925
Yes, it is.

31:28.063 --> 31:29.679
I...

31:31.983 --> 31:33.975
I can't.

31:34.069 --> 31:37.228
- Yes, you can.
- No, I can't!

31:45.413 --> 31:47.280
I don't know how.

31:47.374 --> 31:50.491
Because you don't know
what's going to happen.

31:51.962 --> 31:54.037
None of us do.

31:55.340 --> 31:58.458
That's why it's called
a "leap of faith", John.

32:01.972 --> 32:04.130
You don't have to be alone.

32:24.411 --> 32:26.110
Jack?

32:30.584 --> 32:32.075
John.

32:40.051 --> 32:41.834
Dude...

32:44.097 --> 32:46.381
What is this place?

32:47.475 --> 32:51.605
- John, where's Jack?
- Jack's gone. I need your help.

32:57.277 --> 32:59.946
- What does it look like?
- It's a breaker box.

33:00.030 --> 33:02.866
There has to be one.
Follow the conduit lines.

33:02.949 --> 33:05.650
Cool, OK. Great. What's a conduit line?

33:06.912 --> 33:09.477
Those tubes. Follow those.

33:25.513 --> 33:27.338
Did you find it?

33:30.685 --> 33:33.052
Depends what you mean by "it".

33:40.070 --> 33:42.906
Here's what we do.
Jin plays dead. You call for help.

33:42.989 --> 33:45.523
Sick prisoner? You serious?

33:45.617 --> 33:48.026
What, you got a better idea, sweetheart?

33:48.995 --> 33:51.362
- Where'd you get that gun, anyway?
- What?

33:51.456 --> 33:53.698
The gun, how'd you get it on the plane?

33:53.792 --> 33:55.992
There was a federal marshal
on the plane.

33:56.086 --> 33:59.412
So, what? You just happened
to have his gun?

33:59.506 --> 34:03.291
Yeah. I'm lucky.
Mike, let's get this thing going.

34:03.385 --> 34:06.221
How come you didn't use it
when they grabbed you?

34:07.639 --> 34:10.590
Guess I was too busy getting hit
in the face with a club.

34:14.729 --> 34:17.430
Why are you suddenly so interested,
cupcake?

34:17.524 --> 34:19.067
- Hey!
- What?

34:19.150 --> 34:20.475
Come on, we gotta...

34:22.612 --> 34:24.854
Back up! Back up!

34:29.494 --> 34:30.526
Coming out.

34:32.163 --> 34:33.946
Coming out!

34:46.052 --> 34:48.127
What happened? Who are they?

35:12.579 --> 35:13.820
Damn!

35:18.251 --> 35:19.794
Stop!

35:22.672 --> 35:24.414
Oh, right.

35:25.508 --> 35:27.959
- The code, yeah?
- What?

35:28.053 --> 35:29.596
Listen carefully.

35:29.679 --> 35:33.548
If by some miracle you get
that computer working, enter the code.

35:33.642 --> 35:37.051
4, 8, 15, 16, 23, 42.
Hit "Execute."

35:37.145 --> 35:39.470
- Again. 4, 8, 15...
- Shut up!

35:40.690 --> 35:43.443
- Sorry?
- Nothing is going to happen.

35:44.402 --> 35:47.603
Some... man takes you down there,

35:47.697 --> 35:51.639
shows you a movie,
and you push a button on faith alone?

35:52.369 --> 35:54.934
Nothing is going to happen!

35:56.456 --> 36:00.199
In about 15 minutes, you're either gonna
be very right or very wrong.

36:00.293 --> 36:02.493
You wanna shoot me? Shoot me.
I'm not...

36:02.587 --> 36:06.529
Why are you running? You don't
even know what you're running from!

36:10.637 --> 36:12.712
I remember you.

36:14.391 --> 36:16.257
Running.

36:18.270 --> 36:20.803
I know you. I met you.

36:20.897 --> 36:24.015
- Stop.
- Los Angeles. I was training, yeah?

36:24.818 --> 36:26.684
- You twisted your ankle.
- Stop.

36:26.778 --> 36:31.105
You're a doctor, right? There was
this girl, you were worried, you said...

36:31.199 --> 36:33.524
You said you failed her.

36:34.953 --> 36:38.237
- That was you.
- It doesn't matter.

36:38.331 --> 36:42.325
- Was she OK? The girl?
- It doesn't matter.

36:42.419 --> 36:44.661
- What happened?
- It doesn't matter.

36:44.754 --> 36:47.664
- How can you say it doesn't...
- I married her!

36:57.017 --> 36:58.591
Right.

37:02.105 --> 37:03.971
Then, you're...

37:05.191 --> 37:07.944
You're not married to her anymore, then.

37:31.843 --> 37:34.377
See you in another life, yeah?

37:50.278 --> 37:52.353
Can you fix it?

37:53.406 --> 37:56.566
This man, whoever he was,
replaced the motherboard.

38:00.372 --> 38:04.032
- The power transformer is blown.
- Don't you need to know why?

38:04.918 --> 38:08.828
All I need to know is that the timer
is counting down to something,

38:09.756 --> 38:12.707
and that this computer
needs to be repaired.

38:12.801 --> 38:15.553
I'm sure you'll tell me why
once I've done so.

38:23.895 --> 38:25.762
Found it!

38:35.574 --> 38:37.231
- What's that?
- Sayid...

38:37.325 --> 38:39.233
I'm working on it.

38:39.327 --> 38:41.569
- You have to...
- I know what I have to do.

38:45.041 --> 38:48.368
Reconnected the processor.
Replaced the transformer.

38:55.260 --> 38:56.918
It's on!

38:57.012 --> 39:00.129
- OK, so what now?
- There was a code, he made me enter it.

39:00.223 --> 39:02.590
- What code?
- Can you remember what it is?

39:04.394 --> 39:07.095
- 4. 8.
- Wait a minute.

39:07.397 --> 39:10.932
- 15. 16.
- Dude, I'm serious, stop!

39:11.026 --> 39:13.810
- This is not the time or the place...
- I think it is!

39:13.904 --> 39:14.936
23.

39:15.030 --> 39:18.064
- We don't even know what it does!
- 32.

39:21.369 --> 39:24.612
You know what? Forget it.
Go ahead. Do your thing.

39:27.417 --> 39:29.575
It's not 32.

39:31.379 --> 39:33.079
It's 42.

39:35.342 --> 39:39.127
He just told me. Desmond.
The last number's 42.

39:40.722 --> 39:42.797
You're sure?

39:42.891 --> 39:45.216
Yeah. I'm sure.

40:06.748 --> 40:08.531
You do it, Jack.

40:11.544 --> 40:13.578
What?

40:14.339 --> 40:16.247
You have to do it.

40:17.801 --> 40:20.793
- You do it yourself, John.
- No, you saw the film, Jack.

40:20.887 --> 40:23.171
This is a two-person job. At least.

40:26.768 --> 40:29.886
- This argument is irrelevant.
- Sayid. Don't.

40:29.980 --> 40:31.929
- Jack.
- Don't. It's not real.

40:32.023 --> 40:34.776
Look, you want to push the button,
do it yourself.

40:34.859 --> 40:38.644
If it's not real, then why are you here?
Why did you come back?

40:39.573 --> 40:42.815
- Why do you find it so hard to believe?
- Why do you find it so easy?

40:42.909 --> 40:45.026
It's never been easy!

40:54.337 --> 40:57.205
Maybe you should just do it.

40:57.299 --> 41:00.708
No. It's a button.

41:03.972 --> 41:06.130
I can't do this alone, Jack.

41:09.477 --> 41:11.469
I don't want to.

41:15.025 --> 41:17.517
It's a leap of faith, Jack.

42:12.791 --> 42:15.074
I'll take the first shift.
